@bank dept:works
// PLACEHOLDERS (the career engineer, 0.61.13): the new head writer replaces these. Works crew at the time clock, said as
// a bubble as you clock in or out (about one time in two). Bubbles: 60 characters is the aim. clock.back is your first
// clock-in after leave or a sick day; clock.late when you clock in 20+ minutes late; clock.auto and career.tip.clock
// are texts (read as data, no voice tokens).

== clock.in
- {hi}. Board's busy today. Tea first?
- Morning shift. Let's see what broke overnight.
- Kettle's on in the tea corner, {nick}.

== clock.out
- That's me done. Mind how you go.
- Another day, another filter.
- Off you go, {nick}. Good shift.

== clock.monday
- Good weekend? Mine went too fast.
- Monday again. How was your weekend?

== clock.friday
- Weekend! Doing anything nice?
- Two days off. I'm going to sleep for one of them.

== clock.back
- Look who's back! We missed you on the board.
- Back at it? Good. The filters missed you.

== clock.late
- Afternoon, {nick}. Only joking. Mostly.
- The board noticed you were late. I didn't.

== clock.auto
- You forgot to clock out. The clock signed you out at 17:00.

== career.tip.clock
- Clock in at the time clock in the Works bay, past the tool wall, when your shift starts, and out when it ends.
